{"parentUuid":"8e4d4882-cb0e-467a-85c2-6f3483db0f2a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c05ae742-b7ea-4081-ac5f-2b7df3580a90","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RMM1Ma1DSaR6b89pV67aRS","type":"tool_result","content":"VISION [informational/ste]  (1050 words, 2 findings)\n  - tic triad: 7 (budget 2) [advisory: data lists of three are fine, only rhetorical triads count]\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\nc232056 Vision: an orchestration control plane; plan: the expedition look","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7f612997-1dec-4e15-b436-3dd5c9e96410","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:12:21.750Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VISION [informational/ste]  (1050 words, 2 findings)\n  - tic triad: 7 (budget 2) [advisory: data lists of three are fine, only rhetorical triads count]\n  - first person low for informational register: 0.0/1k words (min 0.5); a standard still needs one or two asides only I can give: why this threshold, what broke first, when I bend it\nc232056 Vision: an orchestration control plane; plan: the expedition look","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":91,"oldLines":6,"newStart":91,"newLines":10,"lines":["   permission points at. Today they live in three places."," - **Lesson.** An escape found after a job landed should become a check, so","   the same miss can't land twice. Verification and the harness meet here.","+- **Field note.** What a job taught, signed by a person when it lands or","+  stops. Together the notes are the atlas.","+- **Outcome.** A job already keeps `criteria`: the summit picked before it","+  leaves. The job page should show it first."," - **Experiment.** An eval is a harness change tried on past requests. A","   rule could offer \"try this on the last 10 requests\" before it goes live."," - **Proposal.** A charter edit is a branch to merge, and a workflow edit is"]},{"oldStart":122,"oldLines":6,"newStart":126,"newLines":48,"lines":[" which version ran. Caveman is the first plugin to try: its skills and its"," prompt hook map onto guidance and a hook."," ","+## The look and feel: an expedition","+","+[The software expedition](https://blog.tacoda.dev/the-software-expedition-ca3631d61530)","+gives the app its picture. Every landmark in it is already a thing in","+Bastion, so the app draws them without new words: a person never has to","+say \"summit\" to use it.","+","+| On the map | In Bastion |","+|---|---|","+| The outpost | Where requests arrive: Jobs, an issue, a schedule |","+| The summit | The outcome a job must reach, picked before it leaves |","+| The guide | The harness: models, tools, the loop |","+| Base camp | The job's worktree and VM |","+| The charter | The workspace's charter (the same word) |","+| The checkpoint | A commit the checks passed |","+| The range of reality | Failing checks, a reviewer, a person sending work back |","+| The final peak | The job lands |","+| The track | The turns and the audit log |","+| Specimens | The change and its artifacts |","+| Field notes | What the job taught, one sentence signed by a person |","+| The marsh | A job stopped or failed, said out loud |","+| The atlas | Everything learned, where the next request starts |","+","+What this changes in the app:","+","+- **A job is a trail, not a list.** The job page draws the route: the","+  workflow's steps as landmarks, each pass back as a peak climbed again,","+  each commit the checks passed as a checkpoint. Where the job is now is a","+  marker on the trail.","+- **Workflows are routes.** Bastion's difference is many workflows, so the","+  Map draws them as routes across a server's ground, from the outpost to","+  the final peak, and a request picks its route at the outpost.","+- **Field notes are a new thing.** When a job lands or stops, a person can","+  sign one sentence: what reality said. A stopped job asks for one, so the","+  marsh is said out loud. Notes feed the atlas, the start of the next","+  request.","+- **A third theme, `bastion-chart`.** The old-world chart's parchment and","+  ink, for people who want the map to look like one. Ink #3b2a1a, paper","+  #efe4c8, red #9b2c1f.","+- **Tactile.** Landmarks are things to press: hover lifts them, a step on","+  the trail opens in place, and a route can be followed with the keys.","+"," ## The layout"," "," ### The bar"]},{"oldStart":210,"oldLines":6,"newStart":256,"newLines":10,"lines":["   be added later. D4 changes."," - Shorter ledes on every page."," ","+### L1b. The chart theme","+","+- `bastion-chart`, beside the first two.","+"," ### L2. The bar"," "," - Seven entries. Insights takes Audit Log, Costs, Evals and Verification as"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":10,"newStart":3,"newLines":13,"lines":[" <!-- voice-register: informational -->"," <!-- voice-english: ste -->"," ","-Bastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and","-a factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,","-and the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a","-job through a workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow","+Bastion is an orchestration control plane for coding agents. Its","+difference is the workflows: you define as many as your work needs, each a","+route of steps with its own people, models and rules, and every request","+picks one. On each server, Bastion manages the harness and the factory","+those routes run on: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent","+works under. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a job along its","+workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow"," says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone. Bastion runs on your"," machine, on a remote server, or on both."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f85bf8e9-1603-4d5a-a265-ce1df44f05b5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8e4d4882-cb0e-467a-85c2-6f3483db0f2a","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
