{"parentUuid":"311a90df-2108-43d2-b645-5af73ca75174","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyit6VuCnY9EsasoJ1bY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done so far, three commits, none pushed:\n\n- **ee37759, themes (part of L1).**\n  - The colors are now a named palette chosen at run time: `bastion-dark` and `bastion-light`. You pick one under Settings › Theme, and the app keeps it for the next start.\n  - About 230 color uses across 32 files moved from constants to theme functions.\n  - I checked both themes in the app: Jobs, the chart, the workflow canvas and Settings all read correctly in light.\n  - CI and the safeguard pass.\n  - I left the app on `bastion-light` after the test. Switch it back in Settings if you prefer dark.\n- **bd7fa2f, then ee37759 and c232056 (plan):**\n  - **Commands are back** as a primitive: a charter's or a plugin's, run by a prompt step. Plugins can carry commands too.\n  - **Vision lede:** \"Bastion is an orchestration control plane for coding agents. Its difference is the workflows: you define as many as your work needs, each a route of steps with its own people, models and rules, and every request picks one.\"\n  - **The expedition as the look and feel.** Medium blocked the fetch, so I read your draft in `all-the-things/drafts/ready/`. Every landmark is already a Bastion thing:\n\n    | On the map | In Bastion |\n    |---|---|\n    | Outpost | Where requests arrive |\n    | Summit | The job's `criteria` |\n    | Guide | The harness |\n    | Base camp | The worktree and VM |\n    | Charter | The charter |\n    | Checkpoint | A commit that passed the checks |\n    | Range of reality | Failing checks, reviewers, a send-back |\n    | Final peak | The job lands |\n    | Track | Turns and the audit log |\n    | Specimens | The change and its artifacts |\n    | Marsh | A job stopped or failed |\n    | Atlas | Everything learned |\n\n  - **What that adds to the plan:**\n    - **The job page as a trail.** The workflow's steps are landmarks, each send-back is a peak climbed again, each commit that passed is a checkpoint, and a marker shows where the job is now.\n    - **Workflows as routes on the Map.** That puts the differentiator in the picture.\n    - **Field notes.** A new entity: one sentence signed by a person when a job lands or stops. A stopped job asks for one. Together the notes form the atlas.\n    - **A third theme, `bastion-chart`,** in your chart's parchment and ink: #efe4c8 paper, #3b2a1a ink, #9b2c1f red. It's phase L1b.\n    - **Expedition words stay in the visuals.** As your post says, nobody has to say \"summit\" at standup.\n\nNext is the rest of L1: plain words across the app (Guidance, Check, Permission, Tool, \"who decides\"), shorter ledes, and a glossary and D4 update in DECISIONS.md. Then L1b, the chart theme. 2.6Gi of disk is free."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1780,"cache_read_input_tokens":541917,"output_tokens":994,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1780,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":994,"cache_read_input_tokens":541917,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1780},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"78af1704-8e4d-4085-8c3d-ecd5f0a3eb52","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgyit67agPYGB9JNSq8Uc","type":"assistant","uuid":"f78b04b1-bdd7-41cc-b50d-0fcf4b62caa3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:12:31.286Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":