{"parentUuid":"d5930fa4-06bf-4393-90d1-32911b9f0b6d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgykuvQim3upLorCyjx1r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Map is done, and the list now pops up in place. Two new commits, neither pushed yet: 0f4052f and fe5e044. The earlier push (`12c3f3e..29717a2`, the trail as a chart) went through.\n\n- **0f4052f, L5 the Map.** It's a new bar entry, `Jobs · Map · Workflows · Workspaces · Harness · Insights · Settings`, with one chart per server.\n  - Workspaces are harbor towns along the coast, each marked \"with its charter\" or \"no charter\".\n  - Each workflow is a dashed red route through its steps (peaks for agent steps, castles for shell steps) to a flagged summit.\n  - A red seal on each step counts the rules on there.\n  - Hovering a step lifts it.\n  - All servers works through the same top-bar switcher.\n- **fe5e044, the popup.** Pressing a landmark opens a card over the chart, right beside it. It flips to the left near the right edge. The card has its own scroll and a Close button, and the page doesn't move. It lists Guidance, Checks and Permissions, each with \"Change on Harness\". I checked it in the app on bug-fix › plan.\n- **Checks:** tests and seams pass, and the safeguard passed before each commit.\n\n**Disk is low again: 428Mi free.** The next build would fail, so I stopped here. Free some space and I'll push and continue. Next:\n- Edit right in the card, instead of linking to Harness.\n- Draw harness items and plugins on the chart.\n- L6, landing per workspace: move the global \"factory lines\" (merge, network, send back) onto each workspace."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":618831,"output_tokens":536,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":201,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":618831,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":201},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b99d3c16-acc7-4173-a5f5-a829e8b4fc82","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgykuurUhiiNYmmKUHnpB","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f84ce90-e1dc-49cc-bcf4-0b2b94cff8c8","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:39:05.964Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
